SYMBOL z_r 80 224 R0
WINDOW 3 18 15 Center 2
WINDOW 0 13 27 Left 2
SYMATTR Value on=1 r=20
SYMATTR InstName R1
TEXT -160 312 Left 2 !.tran 1
TEXT -160 288 Left 2 !.options vntol=0.001 abstol=0.001\n.param vfactor=1 sfactor=1
TEXT -192 -48 Left 2 ;This simple ( linear ) example shows a voltage source and a pure resistive impedance\nOf course this example can also ( simpler ) be simulated with standard spice \nanalysis and components. But nonlinear loadflow analysis ( with constant - power - elements ) \ncan only be done with special ( 4 port ) devices ! -> see the .doc - files for more details
TEXT -168 392 Left 2 ;Note : Since all measurement-output-nodes are voltage nodes all results are in unit Volt [V]\nOf course this is only correct for voltage outputs ( v1_m , z_v1_m ) but not correct for  real and imag power outputs\nlike p1_m , q1_m (HINT: You can multiply the trace in the waveformviewer with *1W/1V to obtain the proper unit)
TEXT -128 120 Left 2 ;v1r = real part of voltage\nv1i = imag part of voltage
TEXT 152 96 Left 2 ;z_p1_m is the real power on the left port of Z_r\nz_q1_m is the imag power on the left port of Z_r\nz_p2_m and z_q2_m are their corresponces for the right port of Z_r\npositive sign means always  - direction into the device
TEXT 240 264 Left 2 ;The real pin of a port of a device is always signed with a "x"\nIf you click with the mouse to the pin you can see the current at this pin\n(real current of x-pin, imag current at non-x-pin)\n \nYou can also get the powerlost if you add z_p1_m and z_p2_m\nSince there is no reactiv power flow through Z_r  -> z_q1_m and z_q2_m are zero
TEXT -192 40 Left 2 ;The additional output nodes for measurement are with suffix "_m"\nAfter simulation you can point with the mouse on these nodes and see the simulated \nresults in the statusline below (.op) or in the waveform viewer (.tran)\nto see at the position of  the measurement pins see also ltspice.lib
TEXT -88 336 Left 2 ;HINT: for 3 phase circuits with absolut values: vfactor=sqrt(3) sfactor=3\nand with 3 phase circuits with per unit (p.u.) values: vfactor=1 sfactor=1
TEXT -168 432 Left 2 ;If you are interested in the macro models of vin and z_r please look also at \nv_r_2.cir
TEXT -168 464 Left 2 ;This schematic ( the symbols vri_slack and  z_r ) needs the macro-library LTSPICE.LIB\nTo see the spice netlist :  Menu - View - SpiceNetlist
TEXT -24 280 Left 2 ;Here you can alter the parameters\nof the models
TEXT 232 160 Left 5 ;!!! Always connect x-pins with x-pins and\nnon-x pins with other pins without x !!!
TEXT -160 280 Left 2 !.param fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}
